GZIP(1)                     User Commands                    GZIP(1)

NAME
    gzip - compress or decompress files in gzip format

SYNOPSIS
    gzip [-cdkt] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    gzip creates standards-compatible gzip streams using DEFLATE fixed
    Huffman coding and LZ77 matching. -d decompresses and verifies streams.

OPTIONS
    -c   write to standard output and preserve input files
    -d   decompress
    -k   retain input files after successful conversion
    -t   test compressed data without writing output

    Compression appends .gz. Decompression removes a final .gz suffix.
    Without files, gzip reads standard input and writes standard output.

SEE ALSO
